A||N||4||burdell1||Scratches on by rear window||||1||
Z||000000||burdell1||12-01-1999||10:37 AM||||Does anyone know if you can take off the black part that is to the left and right of the rear window (right by the rear air vents)? I have scratched mine by taking the rear air vents on and off and wanted to repaint them with matte black paint.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Sage||12-01-1999||10:55 AM||||If you are talking about a GT (fastback) and are reffering to the panels that fit up inside the back of the roof that your vents "tab" into, yes they come off.  There is a phillips head screw at the very back, and under the vents, there should be two 10mm bolts on each side.  Remove these three fastners, and they should come out.  I have seen some that also have a screw up under the roof overhang back edge, but I believe somebody added these, cause they broke the slide holders, getting the panels out.  If you are talking an SE (nothchback), have never taken these off, but would guess it's pretty close to the same mount system, but really don't know for sure.  If you go to the pontiac dealer, they should be able to provide you with a computer printout showing how this assembly is put together.  Good luck!||||reg||1
Z||000002||burdell1||12-01-1999||11:08 AM||||Mine is a '85 GT (notchback)<BR>||||reg||10
Z||000003||TOM||12-01-1999||11:30 AM||||The black triangle things near the back window come off with the removal of I think two screwes on the bottom and a plug on the top under the lip.||||reg||1
Z||000004||RFMike||12-02-1999||11:44 PM||||If the scratches aren't too deep, you can polish them out with mirro-glaze.  I think Big Wheel has it.  I've used it to polish scratches on my cycle fairing.  If it's deep, you can minimize it, but it won't take it out (too mutch material).<BR>||||reg||1
